/*
 | AUTH SOCIAL TEST — PREFAB INITIALIZATION OPTIONS
 |
 | Core always discovers compatible modules automatically. This sample uses a
 | mock social provider so the OAuth flow can be tested without real credentials.
 |
 | Preferred normal setup:
 |
 |   // $prefab = \Tihloh\Prefab\Core\Prefab::create(['db' => $pdo]);
 |
 | Social providers are explicit only because client credentials/provider SDKs
 | are project-specific. Adding one does not disable discovery of other modules.
 |
 | Example custom social provider setup:
 |
 |   // $google = new MyGoogleSocialProvider(
 |   //     clientId: $_ENV['GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID'],
 |   //     clientSecret: $_ENV['GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET'],
 |   //     redirectUri: $_ENV['APP_URL'].'/auth/google/callback',
 |   // );
 |   // $socialProviders->register($google);
 |
 | If Users already exists, Auth/Social should reuse it where possible. If Logs
 | exists, social login/link/unlink activity should integrate automatically.
 |
 | Explicit Auth/Social initialization is required only for provider/session/user
 | resolver details that Prefab cannot infer from existing modules/defaults.
 */
